  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would, by virtue of its considerable scale, particularly its depth and height, and its setting at a raised level appear unduly dominant and out of keeping with the character and appearance of the garden scene and the surrounding area. As such the proposed development fails to comply with Policy 26 of the Havering Local Plan (adopted 2021) and the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (2011).",
    "The proposed development, due to its scale and setting at a raised level would appear as overbearing to the neighbouring occupants at Nos.47 and 51 Carlisle Road and No.6 King's Road; and would give rise to overlooking towards Nos. 47 and 51 King's Road private amenity space. As a result, the proposed development contradicts with Policy 7 of the Havering Local Plan (adopted 2021) and the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (2011).",
    "Refusal Informative",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy a decision was made on the application, which will enable the applicant to exercise a right of appeal if they so wish.",
    "You are advised that any future application must be supported by a personal statement stating the relationship of the applicant and the occupier(s) of the annex."
  ],
